  "live_records": {
    "q-60866": {
      "dom_id": "step-q60866",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193754/assets/2686294e02363c606d70d2993a194978d8d5579202d7ac5732297f74207b21e8.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $f(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a mapping diagram, the range consists of all the outputs to which an arrow is drawn.\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{1,2\\}.$",
